Game Boy Pokémon companion tests (the kiwami fork of BananaOS)

fixtures/ holds PokeDaisy's RAM captures of Gold, Silver and Crystal (and from step 12 of the plan, Red, Blue and
Yellow), copied unchanged from PokeDaisy's app/src/test/resources/fixtures/ at commit 135ac809: each folder a moment of
a game, as the emulated console's memory had it (wram.bin C000-DFFF as the bus had it, hram.bin FF80-FFFE, and for the
Color games wramx.bin, the eight WRAM banks, 0x1000 each), with PokeDaisy's README.txt saying what the moment is.
kiwami/tests/gbpk-units.cpp replays them to the companion's reader. Like any RAM dump they hold a few kilobytes the game
copied there from its ROM; the saves in them are new games PokeDaisy's author played headless.

made-up/ is the fork's own (made-up ROMs and archives, kiwami/tests/gbpk/made-up/make-fixtures.sh).

